      <p>University of Southern Indiana</p>
      <h3>PROPOSALS OVERVIEW</h3>
      <p>Energy Systems Group Inc. (ESGI) and Johnson Controls, Inc. have been invited by the University of Southern Indiana to evaluate campus energy needs and propose facility upgrades. The evaluation was to have three primary objectives:</p>
      <ol>
        <li>Address specific projects or problem areas provided by the University.</li>
        <li>Identify other areas of opportunity for facility upgrades that pay for themselves.</li>
        <li>Design a long range utilities plan in conjunction with existing campus master plan for growth.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>Together we delivered a detailed 3-Phase Proposal to the University for consideration on <span data-field="proposal_date_1">{{ proposal_date_1 }}</span>. The proposed retrofits for the individual buildings were developed by Johnson Controls, Inc. and ESGI developed the central distribution system and the Physical Plant. This document finalizes the first phase.</p>
      <p>The Scope of this Proposal includes upgrades that will beneficially affect the campus' electrical power, lighting, heating, and cooling. The proposed upgrades to the Physical Plant and the other building improvements enhance the University's existing assets. The result is the first step towards a thermally balanced, integrated utilities system which will deliver services at the lowest operation and maintenance budget levels while accruing savings during daily production. Some of the benefits to the University include:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Total energy savings over <span data-field="energy_savings_amount">{{ energy_savings_amount }}</span>.</li>
        <li>Lower utilities cost at the Apartments.</li>
        <li>Over <span data-field="cooling_capacity">{{ cooling_capacity }}</span> of additional cooling capacity through thermal storage.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>This project optimizes the campus central utilities plant. Modernization is the foundation of our proposed integrated utilities system and integral to any long range Master Plan. These changes, along with the other proposed improvements, form a utility infrastructure that will meet today's operating needs and tomorrow's growth needs.</p>
      <p style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <img src="placeholder_signature" alt="Signature" style="width: 150px; float: left; margin-right: 20px;">
        <span data-field="signer_name">{{ signer_name }}</span>, Energy Systems Group
      </p>
    </div>
